WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.635
Every step of a workflow is an activity, and your module can add its own.

00:00:05.635 --> 00:00:10.269
Let's read the Notify Task activity of the Workflows module part by part:

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:13.789
its class, its editor, its views and its registration.

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:16.840
Then let's find them in the workflow designer.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.205
A workflow is a set of activities connected to each other.

00:00:25.205 --> 00:00:27.675
A task does some work and continues.

00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:33.440
An event halts the workflow until something happens, and only an event can start a workflow.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.317
Each activity returns outcomes, which are named exits such as Done.

00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:42.841
The designer draws a port for each outcome, and a transition connects that

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.650
port to the next activity.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.002
A task with settings needs an activity class, a display driver with its

00:00:50.002 --> 00:00:53.708
view model, three views, and one call that registers it.

00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:58.430
The Notify Task of the Workflows module has every part, so let's read it.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:08.628
NotifyTask derives from TaskActivity, passing its own type, which sets the activity's Name

00:01:08.628 --> 00:01:10.128
to the class name.

00:01:10.128 --> 00:01:14.002
Workflow definitions refer to the activity by that name.

00:01:14.002 --> 00:01:22.500
IActivityDescription declares the display name and the category as localization sources, which DisplayText and Category translate.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.978
The constructor asks for the services the activity needs.

00:01:26.978 --> 00:01:33.369
Activities are created with constructor injection, so NotifyTask receives the notifier, the expression

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:35.440
evaluator and the localizers.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:41.376
Settings are properties that read and write through GetProperty and SetProperty.

00:01:41.376 --> 00:01:47.407
The values are stored by property name in the activity's Properties, which the workflow saves.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:52.050
Message is a WorkflowExpression, evaluated each time the activity runs.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.356
GetPossibleOutcomes lists the outcomes, here only Done.

00:01:56.356 --> 00:01:58.279
ExecuteAsync does the work:

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:03.351
it evaluates the message, adds the notification, and returns the outcome by name.

00:02:03.351 --> 00:02:06.790
The workflow follows the transitions of that outcome.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:17.145
The display driver derives from ActivityDisplayDriver, with the activity and a view model.

00:02:17.145 --> 00:02:24.133
EditActivity copies the settings into the view model, and UpdateActivity copies the posted values back.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.800
Message is required.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:30.873
The base class builds three shapes named after the activity class:

00:02:30.873 --> 00:02:32.855
Thumbnail, Design and Edit.

00:02:32.855 --> 00:02:37.418
You write one Razor view for each, and the Workflows module keeps them

00:02:37.418 --> 00:02:39.700
in the Items folder under Views.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.641
The Thumbnail view is the card of the activity in the Activities pane:

00:02:44.641 --> 00:02:46.405
a title and a description.

00:02:46.405 --> 00:02:50.320
The designer replaces the icon at the start of the title with the

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.140
icon from the registration.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.628
The Design view is the body of the activity on the canvas.

00:02:56.628 --> 00:03:00.949
It shows the notification type as a title, unless the Title field is

00:03:00.949 --> 00:03:03.110
set, and the message in quotes.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.878
The Edit view holds only your own settings:

00:03:06.878 --> 00:03:09.589
a label, an input and a hint for each.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:13.531
The module adds a Title field before it and, for a task, a

00:03:13.531 --> 00:03:15.810
When it fails section after it.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.951
A setting that takes an expression in a choice of syntaxes uses a

00:03:23.951 --> 00:03:26.616
WorkflowExpressionInput in its view model.

00:03:26.616 --> 00:03:32.611
The driver reads it back with the WorkflowExpressionInputValidator, which reports a missing expression

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.720
or a syntax that is not allowed.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:42.811
In the Edit view, CreateWorkflowExpressionEditorAsync builds the WorkflowExpressionEditor shape from the bound property.

00:03:42.811 --> 00:03:47.880
It shows the syntax and the expression together, with the label and hint you set.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:59.428
AddActivity registers the activity and its display driver, in the ConfigureServices method of a Startup class.

00:03:59.428 --> 00:04:02.469
The optional icon is a Font Awesome class.

00:04:02.469 --> 00:04:07.220
Without one, the designer uses the category's icon, or a generic one.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:14.036
Your module's feature depends on OrchardCore.Workflows, as the Timers feature does, and registers

00:04:14.036 --> 00:04:16.156
its activities in its Startup.

00:04:16.156 --> 00:04:21.574
A module that works without workflows marks a Startup with RequireFeatures instead, as

00:04:21.574 --> 00:04:23.400
the Contents module does.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:31.265
Let's find the three views in the workflow designer.

00:04:31.265 --> 00:04:38.078
Under Design, Workflows, we open Notify editors, a workflow that starts with a Content Published Event.

00:04:38.078 --> 00:04:42.140
A separate video covers building workflows in the designer.

00:04:42.603 --> 00:04:45.549
In the Activities pane, let's search for notify.

00:04:45.549 --> 00:04:49.533
Under UI, the category from the class, the card shows the bell icon

00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:53.953
from the registration, and the title and description of the Thumbnail view.

00:04:54.406 --> 00:04:56.351
Let's add it after the event.

00:04:56.351 --> 00:05:00.799
Clicking the Done port opens a list of activities, and picking Notify Task

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:03.356
adds it to the right, already connected.

00:05:03.862 --> 00:05:07.371
The header shows the display text, Notify Task.

00:05:07.371 --> 00:05:09.623
The body is the Design view:

00:05:09.623 --> 00:05:14.523
a Success Notification title, and the message in quotes, left empty.

00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:18.762
The node also shows an issue, because Message is required.

00:05:19.246 --> 00:05:24.063
The designer opens the settings of an added activity at the bottom of the canvas.

00:05:24.063 --> 00:05:25.613
That is the Edit view:

00:05:25.613 --> 00:05:30.153
Notification Type and Message, with the Title field before them and the When

00:05:30.153 --> 00:05:32.036
it fails section after them.

00:05:32.505 --> 00:05:35.373
Let's choose Information and type a message.

00:05:35.373 --> 00:05:40.020
When the field loses focus, the designer applies the change, and the Design

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.405
view shows Information Notification with the message.

00:05:47.605 --> 00:05:53.668
An event derives from EventActivity instead, as this one from the Data Pipelines module does.

00:05:53.668 --> 00:05:58.996
The base class's Execute method halts the workflow, and the event's Resume method

00:05:58.996 --> 00:06:01.078
runs when the event arrives.

00:06:01.078 --> 00:06:05.365
EventActivity isn't generic, so the event overrides Name itself.

00:06:06.115 --> 00:06:11.860
Your code triggers the event by calling TriggerEventAsync on IWorkflowManager, with the activity's

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.794
name and an input dictionary.

00:06:13.794 --> 00:06:18.214
The call starts the workflows that begin with the event, and resumes those

00:06:18.214 --> 00:06:19.485
that wait for it.

00:06:21.485 --> 00:06:25.666
A task activity is a class, a display driver with a view model,

00:06:25.666 --> 00:06:28.030
three views and one registration.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.909
An event follows the same shape and waits to be triggered.

00:06:31.909 --> 00:06:33.485
Thanks for watching.

